                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's worth the $3 asking price. It's a \"collect the coins and other collectible stuff\" platformer that makes strong use of the Z axis. It's fairly forgiving of mistakes; you don't insta-die if you miss a jump. The environments are attractive, movement is fluid and performance good. I liked the music. It has skill trees. You can throw bombs and change into a wolf. The grumbling gnome voice (not sure if he's speaking a slavic language or sim-speak meant to sound like a slavic language) is well done, and he complains a lot, so he has a fair bit of personality. The game does have its rough spots:   It only supports keyboard + mouse, and the controls cannot be remapped; press G (or K, I forget which is the skill tree and which is the options menu) in game to see what they are. Combat is clumsy because of inability to remap keys, as well as the fact that your swings are on a timer; you can't madly click the mouse to hack away, which leads to a run up, swing, dash away mechanic. English translations of fairly limited text were obviously done by a non-native speaker.\n\nIn sum, I think the game is better than it has been marketed. A lot of effort obviously went into it.",
